# GTM Launch Strategy — {{ brand_name or name or "Brand" }}

## Best current motion
One opinionated sentence naming the selected primary motion and any secondary motion with its unlock condition.

## Why this motion
Write the full reasoning for the motion selection. This section must do four things:

1. Name the specific buyer-map signals that determined this motion. Quote the loaded buyer_map.v1 fields directly: awareness_level, buyer_type, dominant_blocking_force, trust_gap, adoption_stage, ACV range. Write "The buyer_map.v1 shows awareness_level: solution_aware" not "the buyer is solution aware". If buyer_map.v1 was not loaded, every signal must be labeled (inferred).

2. Eliminate the alternatives explicitly. For each motion that was considered and rejected, name it and explain the specific reason it fails for this buyer at this stage. "Content-led was eliminated because..." "Paid-first was eliminated because..." A business leader reading this should know exactly why every other motion was ruled out before this one was selected.

3. Name what this motion requires to be true about the company — what capability, what network, what resource — and whether that condition is currently met or assumed.

4. Name the failure mode: what breaks first if this motion is wrong, and what signal would appear before revenue confirms it.

## Primary audience
One focused paragraph identifying the most likely first audience or ICP segment. Be specific from context — not demographic labels but a description of the situation this person is in, what they have already tried, and what makes them ready to act now. If inferred, state that clearly and name what client signal would sharpen it.

## Positioning angle
One sharp positioning line for the launch.

## Core promise
One sentence describing the outcome the offer helps the audience achieve.

## Launch sequence
Write each stage as a short paragraph. Each paragraph must cover: what happens in this stage, why this order (what breaks if this stage is skipped), what the completion signal looks like in practice, and what failure at this stage tells you about the strategy.

Do not use the format `Stage N: Label — what gets done — what it unlocks — completion signal` as a single line. That format collapses the reasoning that makes this section trustworthy.

Stage 0 — Foundation
[paragraph]

Stage 1 — Proof and first conversations
[paragraph]

Stage 2 — Conversion path validation
[paragraph]

Stage 3 — Proof-building and message refinement
[paragraph]

Stage 4 — Channel expansion
Pending gate: [state the specific gate condition that must be met before this stage is elaborated]

Stage 5 — Scale
Pending gate: [state the specific gate condition that must be met before this stage is elaborated]

## Channel stack

### Do now
Maximum three channels. Only include channels whose prerequisites are present in loaded context or directly created by Stage 0.

Every channel entry MUST use exactly this format. No bullet points. No `*` or `-` prefixes. No inline dashes. The channel name on its own bold line, then Decision, then Rationale — nothing else:

**[Channel name]**
Decision: [actual channel role e.g. acquisition / conversion hub / intent capture / trust-building] — [specific buyer_map.v1 field and value e.g. dominant_blocking_force: anxiety] — [what proof is required before this channel can scale]
Rationale: [One to two sentences of prose. Name the specific buyer behavior on this surface and why it fits this buyer at this awareness level. Do not repeat the Decision line — add the reasoning behind it.]

Replace every bracket placeholder with an actual value. "role", "buyer-map signal", and "proof required" are field labels — never write them literally in the output.
The Decision line buyer-map value must come from the loaded buyer_map.v1 (e.g. `awareness_level: solution_aware`, `dominant_blocking_force: anxiety`, `trust_gap: integration proof`). Do not invent a signal that is not in the loaded map.

### Hold
Use bullets. Each line must be `Channel — hold reason — specific unlock condition`.
The unlock condition must be precise enough to act on. "Hold until proof assets exist" is not acceptable. "Hold until one named case study from a comparable [specific client type] exists" is.
- Channel — hold reason — specific unlock condition

### Avoid for now
Use bullets. Each line must be `Channel — avoid reason referencing buyer-map signal`.
The avoid reason must reference the buyer map — wrong buyer type, wrong awareness level, wrong ACV, wrong proof requirement. "High cost" alone is not a buyer-map reason.
- Channel — avoid reason

## Conversion path
Use numbered steps. Each line must be `Touchpoint — message job — action required — advance signal — blocking force addressed`.

## First proof assets needed
Use bullets. Each line must be `Trust gap — proof format — available now or unlock stage — channel or artifact`.
- Trust gap — proof format — available now or unlock stage — channel or artifact

## Measurement frame
Use bullets. Define leading indicators and gates without numeric targets unless a baseline exists in the loaded reports.
- Stage — leading indicators — numeric targets: requires baseline — review cadence — gate condition

## Assumptions I made
Each assumption must include three things written as a short block:
- What we believe to be true
- What changes about the strategy if this is wrong — specifically which section of the plan breaks and how
- How the business leader can test this: what they would look at in their own sales data, customer conversations, or operations to confirm or correct it

Do not write single-line assumption bullets. Each assumption block should be three to five sentences minimum.

## Critical gaps
For each gap, write a short paragraph — not a bullet line — that explains: what is missing, what part of the strategy is exposed until this gap is filled, and what executing without filling it produces as a failure mode. A critical gap is not just an item to collect. It is a strategic liability that changes the confidence of the plan.

## Useful later
Use bullets. Non-blocking inputs that would improve fidelity at later stages.
- Input

## Next artifacts
Use bullets. Each line must be `Artifact — purpose — which stage it enables`.
- Artifact — purpose — stage it enables

## Approval note
One sentence: this is a draft strategy for review; execution artifacts, publishing, outreach, spend, and external platform actions require separate approval.
